.TH QFW-TARGET 1 "November 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Commands"
.SH NAME
qfw-target \- print what a QPM says about its device, without reserving it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qfw-target
.RI [ --run-dir " directory" ]
.RI [ --provider " name" ]
.RI [ --service-id " id" ]
.RI [ --lib " library" ]
.RI [ --timeout " seconds" ]
.RI [ --output " file" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw-target
resolves one QPM in the runtime prepared by
.BR qfw-setup (1)
the way
.B QFwBackend
does, and reads its telemetry. It does not reserve the QPM. In a job with a
reservation it describes the reserved QPM. Otherwise
.B QFW_QPM_IMPL
picks the provider when
.B --provider
is not given.
It runs on the current node with the same DEFw environment
.BR qfw-srun (1)
gives an application.
.PP
It prints one
.B qfw-target-v1
JSON object:
.TP
.B schema
.BR qfw-target-v1 .
.TP
.B service_id
The resolved service.
.TP
.B provider
The service's provider.
.TP
.B settings
The properties the service publishes in the directory, such as
.BR num_qubits ,
and for the
.B aer
provider
.BR aer_mode ,
.B aer_device
and
.BR aer_method .
.TP
.BR backend_info ", " device_info ", " coupling_graph ", " calibration
The QPM's telemetry records. A record the QPM cannot answer is null, and
.B errors
holds the error's message.
.PP
.B qfw_qiskit.qfw_target_query.target_from_json
builds the Qiskit target from the document, as
.B QFwBackend
builds it from the same records. A QPM that describes no device gets the same
generic 400-qubit target as the backend.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --run-dir " directory"
The application run directory; as for
.BR qfw-srun (1)
when omitted.
.TP
.BI --provider " name"
Resolve a service of this provider.
.TP
.BI --service-id " id"
Resolve this service. The name of a QPM that
.BR qfw-setup (1)
launched for the run resolves to its runtime id.
.TP
.BI --lib " library"
The shim library to describe. The default is
.BR QFW_SHIM_LIB .
.TP
.BI --timeout " seconds"
How long to wait for the directory and for a matching service. The default
is 10. DEFw can take several seconds to reach the directory.
.TP
.BI --output " file"
Write the document to this file instead of standard output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero when the document was written. Nonzero when the runtime is not ready or
no service matches, with the reason on one line of standard error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-setup (1),
.BR qfw-srun (1),
.BR qfw-status (1),
.BR qfw-services.yaml (5),
.BR qfw (7)
